  "body": "Literally start your day watching the sun lift over Rangitoto Island, stroll to Torbay Village for coffee, or push your kayak out onto a glassy Gulf. Welcome to 4 Auld Street, a boutique collection of five brand-new, free-standing and freehold homes designed for growing and multi-generation families wanting space, privacy and a coastal lifestyle in an established, leafy pocket of central Torbay, where the soundtrack is birdsong.\r\n\r\nEvery home enjoys sea views, from sweeping panoramas across the Hauraki Gulf to a peaceful outlook over treetops to the water.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, high stud ceilings, designer skylights and oversized windows fill the living areas with natural light and frame the views. High-spec kitchens with island benches, light beach-toned flooring and easy flow to sunny balconies create a relaxed setting for everyday family life.\r\n\r\nDownstairs is all about flexibility, with generous bedrooms and bathrooms providing privacy for teenagers or visiting guests, space to work from home, and a private deck and garden to enjoy. Double internal access garage, generous off-street parking and an extra-wide driveway make coming home easy, while a 10-Year Master Build Guarantee brings lasting peace of mind.\r\n\r\nEnjoy an easy stroll to your local shops and cafés, swim and picnic at Long Bay Regional Park, launch your boat or kayak just down the road at Waiake Beach, even learn to sail at the Torbay Sailing Club. Zoned for Torbay School, Northcross Intermediate and Long Bay College.\r\n\r\n•\t4A (Lot 1): The showpiece, offering the most space and the most commanding panoramic sea and city views. Approx. 182m² gross building area on 232m² of freehold land.\r\n•\t4B (Lot 2): Bright, beautifully balanced and exceptional value. Approx. 175m² gross building area on 188m² of freehold land.\r\n•\t4C (Lot 3): Sun-filled, easy-care and designed for practical everyday living. Approx. 174m² gross building area on 188m² of freehold land.\r\n•\t4D (Lot 4): Two living areas, landscaped gardens and space to work from home. Approx. 168m² gross building area on 188m² of freehold land.\r\n•\t4E (Lot 5): The private end home, with the largest backyard and extra off-street parking for three vehicles. Approx. 180m² gross building area on 215m² of freehold land.\r\n\r\nBrand-new family homes of this quality, so close to the sand, rarely come along. The seller has given clear instructions to sell. Enquire today and secure your spacious new home for summer!",
